# Loading and empty states

Import from `@webonone/ui-kit`: **`LoadingState`**, **`ItemListEmpty`**.

## Unified platform loading overlay (required)

**WebOnOne core, Data, Email, and new platform-shell satellites** must show **one** viewport overlay for session, lazy-route, and page/data loads — never stacked spinners on refresh.

```text
AppLayout
  PlatformLoadingProvider
  → always render <Outlet />
  → single <LoadingState key="platform-loading" overlay label={…} />
SessionRoleGate / session hooks → usePlatformLoading('Loading session…')
LazyRoute Suspense fallback → useRouteLoading('Loading page…'); return null
Pages / list fetches → usePlatformLoading(loading ? 'Loading …' : null)
```

| Hook / surface | Role |
|----------------|------|
| `PlatformLoadingProvider` | Wrap `AppLayout` content tree |
| `usePlatformLoading(label)` | Session gate, page data fetch, editor load |
| `useRouteLoading(label)` | Lazy route chunk (`LazyRoute` only) |
| `AppLayout` overlay | Sole visible loading UI |

Hooks use **`useLayoutEffect`** to set/clear labels (avoids one-frame overlay gaps).

**Label priority**

| App | `overlayLabel` |
|-----|----------------|
| Data / Email satellite | `sessionLoading ? 'Loading session…' : pageLabel ?? routeLabel` |
| WebOnOne core | `pageLabel ?? routeLabel` (session via `SessionRoleGate` → `usePlatformLoading`) |

Context module (same API — copy per service):

| Service | Path |
|---------|------|
| WebOnOne v2 | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/shell/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx` |
| Data / Email | `<service>/frontend/src/features/auth/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx` |

Reference: `data/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `data/frontend/src/app/LazyRoute.tsx`, `webonone-v2/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/session/components/SessionRoleGate.tsx`.

**Forbidden:** inline `"Loading…"` text in pages; per-page `<LoadingState overlay />`; `LazyRoute` fallback that renders visible `Spinner`/`LoadingState`; second overlay during `RoleRoute` handoff (return `null` — overlay handles it).

**Exception:** platform inbound **`code` bootstrap** on the destination **home page** may show a page-content spinner during exchange only — not a second AppLayout overlay. See [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc).

## LoadingState (AppLayout + buttons)

Centered themed spinner + label.

| Prop | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `label` | Contextual: `"Loading tags…"`, `"Loading session…"`, `"Loading page…"` |
| `overlay` | **`true`** in **`AppLayout` only** — nowhere else |

**Buttons:** **`Spinner size="sm"`** inside the button — not `LoadingState`.

Page hook example: `data/frontend/src/features/tags/pages/TagsPage.tsx`.

## ItemListEmpty

Centered empty-list message when **`items.length === 0`** inside or instead of `ItemList`.

Pass copy as children, e.g. `<ItemListEmpty>No tags found.</ItemListEmpty>`.

Reference: `data/frontend/src/features/tags/components/TagsList.tsx`.

## Verification

```bash
npm run build -w @webonone/ui-kit
npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root
npm run type-check -w data-root
npm run type-check -w email-root
```

